# base/host.manifest -- the ship-list every HOST target shares.
#
# [P251] EXTRACTED 2026-09-28 from six byte-identical manifests: linux_x86_64_bc,
# linux_x86_64_floatprof, linux_x86_64_ncg, linux_x86_64_poison, wasm32_wasi, windows_x86_64.
# Four more (linux_aarch64_cuda, linux_x86_64, linux_x86_64_hip, linux_x86_64_profile) were
# identical to these EXCEPT for one line -- features/llip-vision.scm -- so ten files existed to
# express two lists, and a one-line difference was stored as a 58-line copy.
#
# A target extending this adds what it DIFFERS by.  Drop an inherited entry with `-<destination>`.
# Nothing here is arch-specific: the name is `host` because these are the non-board targets, and a
# board manifest should NOT extend it -- the board lists are genuinely different, not duplicated.
